# ArthNiti — SIH 2026
#
# Two rules before adding a pattern:
#   1. Never ignore anything a teammate needs to receive. Six people share this
#      repo; an over-broad pattern silently hides someone's work.
#   2. Adding a pattern does NOT untrack an already-tracked file. That needs a
#      deliberate `git rm --cached <path>`.

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Virtual environments. The live one is ./.venv (Python 3.14.6); ./backend/venv
# is an older second one. "venv/" alone does NOT match ".venv/" — the leading dot
# defeats it — which is why both forms are listed. Until now .venv escaped git
# only because the venv module writes its own .gitignore containing "*" inside it.
.venv/
venv/

# Test and lint caches. Same story as .venv: .pytest_cache was self-ignoring via
# a generated file rather than by our rules.
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---- Node and frontend build ----
# frontend/.gitignore covers the Vite defaults. These repeat the important ones
# so an install or build run from the repo root is covered too.
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
.vite/
*.local

# ---- Secrets ----
# The MVP has no API keys and no .env today: there is no LLM and no database.
# This stays so the first key anyone adds is ignored by default instead of
# pushed to a repo six people pull from. .env.example stays shareable.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- Logs ----
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ---- Editors and OS ----
# .vscode/settings.json is already tracked and shared with the team, so the
# star form is deliberate: ".vscode/*" excludes the folder's CONTENTS, which
# leaves the negations below able to rescue individual files. A bare
# ".vscode/" would exclude the directory itself and the negations would fail.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.sw?
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---- Assistant / agent local state ----
.claude/

# ---- Heavy demo artefacts, kept local ----
# 27 full-page PNGs at 2880px, regenerated on demand. Hand them to teammates as
# a zip rather than through the repo.
screenshots/

# ---- Local data and model files ----
# None exist today. Keeps stray binaries out by default.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.pkl

# NOTE: presentation/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Saad and Tripti need the deck
# to reach the whole team through the repo.
